      <div class="amount">$599&ndash;$899</div>
      <div class="monthly">Optional care: $75&ndash;$129/month</div>
    </div>

    <div class="price-card">
      <h3>Automation</h3>
      <div class="amount">$699&ndash;$1,200+</div>
      <div class="monthly">Optional care: $99&ndash;$199+/month</div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <p class="price-note">
    Prices are estimates based on project requirements.
    Hosting, domain registration, premium software,
    and third-party subscriptions may involve additional costs.
  </p>

  <!-- PRICING FAQ -->

  <h2 class="section-title">Pricing &amp; Payments</h2>

  <div class="faq-group">

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>How much does a website cost?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>WebRite website packages start at <strong>$199</strong> for a simple online presence.</p>
        <p>More advanced websites with multiple pages, lead generation tools, booking systems, or business automation typically cost more.</p>
        <p>You can receive a personalized estimate through our <a href="/get-a-quote">Get a Quote</a> page.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Are there monthly fees?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Monthly website care is optional and depends on the services you need.</p>
        <p>Maintenance plans can include website updates, content changes, technical assistance, and support for connected automation tools.</p>
        <p>Separate hosting, domain, or third-party service charges may still apply.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Do I have to pay everything upfront?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Payment arrangements are discussed before work begins. Your project quote will outline the total cost, payment schedule, and included services.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can I upgrade my website later?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Absolutely. Your website can evolve as your business grows.</p>
        <p>Additional pages, contact forms, appointment booking, automated notifications, and other features can be discussed after launch.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

  </div>

  <!-- OWNERSHIP -->

  <h2 class="section-title">Ownership &amp; Hosting</h2>

  <div class="faq-group">

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Will I own my website?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Your agreement will specify ownership of the completed website, original content, and design assets.</p>
        <p>You maintain ownership of your business domain when it is registered in your name or account. Third-party platforms and software remain subject to their respective licensing terms.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Do I need to purchase a domain name?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>A custom domain is recommended for a professional business website.</p>
        <p>If you already own a domain, WebRite can help connect it to your new website.</p>
        <p>If you don't have one, we can guide you through selecting and registering a domain.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>What is website hosting?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Website hosting is the service that makes your website accessible on the internet.</p>
        <p>Depending on your project, your website may use a managed website platform or a separate hosting provider.</p>
        <p>We'll discuss the appropriate setup before development.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can I use my existing hosting provider?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>In many cases, yes. Compatibility depends on the platform and features your website requires.</p>
        <p>WebRite can review your existing setup before recommending changes.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

  </div>

  <!-- DEVELOPMENT -->

  <h2 class="section-title">Website Design &amp; Development</h2>

  <div class="faq-group">

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>How long does it take to build a website?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Timelines depend on the number of pages, design requirements, and requested functionality.</p>
        <p>A simple website can often be completed faster than a larger project involving booking systems, integrations, or automation.</p>
        <p>You'll receive a projected timeline before development begins.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Will my website work on mobile phones?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Yes. WebRite designs responsive websites that adapt to desktop computers, tablets, and smartphones.</p>
        <p>Mobile usability is an important part of the development process.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can you redesign my existing website?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Yes. WebRite can help modernize an existing website's appearance, navigation, content structure, and functionality.</p>
        <p>The scope depends on your current platform and the changes you want to make.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Do I need to provide the website content?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>You'll need to provide important business details such as your services, contact information, preferred branding, and any required policies.</p>
        <p>WebRite can assist with organizing and refining website copy as part of the project scope.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can I request changes during development?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Yes. Your project agreement will explain the review process and included revisions.</p>
        <p>Major changes outside the original scope may require an updated quote.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

  </div>

  <!-- AUTOMATION -->

  <h2 class="section-title">Automation &amp; Business Tools</h2>

  <div class="faq-group">

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>What is website automation?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Website automation connects your website to tools that perform repetitive tasks with less manual involvement.</p>
        <p>Examples include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Automatic customer inquiry notifications</li>
          <li>Appointment booking workflows</li>
          <li>Instant estimate calculators</li>
          <li>Lead collection and organization</li>
          <li>Automated email or SMS responses</li>
          <li>Customer intake forms</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can you connect my website to Google Forms?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Yes. Google Forms can be integrated into supported website workflows for collecting inquiries, applications, and customer information.</p>
        <p>Depending on your requirements, collected data may also be organized through Google Sheets or connected automation services.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can my website send text message notifications?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Yes. Supported SMS integrations can notify you when customers submit forms, request appointments, or make inquiries.</p>
        <p>SMS functionality may require a third-party provider and additional usage fees.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can you add AI to my website?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>AI-powered features may be available depending on your business needs and the platform used.</p>
        <p>Potential applications include automated customer responses, lead qualification, appointment assistance, and information collection.</p>
        <p>These features are quoted separately based on their complexity and ongoing service requirements.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can my website accept payments?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Payment processing can be integrated into supported website platforms.</p>
        <p>Depending on your business, this may include deposits, service payments, or customer checkout.</p>
        <p>Payment providers typically charge their own transaction fees.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

  </div>

  <!-- SUPPORT -->

  <h2 class="section-title">Support &amp; Working With WebRite</h2>

  <div class="faq-group">

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Who will actually build my website?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>You'll work directly with WebRite's founder throughout the website development process.</p>
        <p>Learn more on our <a href="/meet-your-builder">Meet Your Builder</a> page.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>What happens after my website launches?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Once your website is completed, we'll review the agreed deliverables and launch requirements.</p>
        <p>If you select an ongoing maintenance plan, WebRite can continue assisting with updates, support, and approved improvements.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Do you only work with businesses in California?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>No. WebRite serves businesses remotely.</p>
        <p>Our primary focus includes Riverside, the Inland Empire, Los Angeles, Orange County, and San Diego, but we can work with businesses throughout the United States.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>How do I get started?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Getting started is simple.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Visit the Get a Quote page.</li>
          <li>Select your preferred website package.</li>
          <li>Choose any additional features.</li>
          <li>Provide your business and contact information.</li>
          <li>Submit your project inquiry for review.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="/get-a-quote">Request Your Website Quote &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

  </div>

  <!-- CTA -->

  <section class="cta">
    <div>
      <h2>Still Have Questions?</h2>
      <p>
        Tell me about your business and what you want
        your website to accomplish. I'll help you
        identify the right starting point.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn" href="/get-a-quote">Get My Quote &rarr;</a>
  </section>

